              "angles": [
                {
                  "at": "O",
                  "label": "40^\\circ"
                },
                {
                  "at": "O",
                  "label": "65^\\circ"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          "answer": "75^\\circ",
          "hint": "Use vertically opposite angles and angles on a straight line.",
          "solution": "Angles on the straight line $AD$ add to $180^\\circ$. So $\\angle FOE = 180^\\circ - (40^\\circ + 65^\\circ) = 75^\\circ$. $\\angle BOC$ is vertically opposite to $\\angle FOE$, so $\\angle BOC = 75^\\circ$.",
          "steps": [
            {
              "explain": "Angles on the straight line \\(AD\\) add to \\(180^\\circ\\).",
              "work": "\\angle AOF + \\angle FOE + \\angle EOD = 180^\\circ"
            },
            {
              "explain": "Substitute known values.",
              "work": "40^\\circ + \\angle FOE + 65^\\circ = 180^\\circ"
            },
            {
              "explain": "Solve for \\(\\angle FOE\\).",
              "work": "\\angle FOE = 180^\\circ - 105^\\circ = 75^\\circ"
            },
            {
              "explain": "\\(\\angle BOC\\) and \\(\\angle FOE\\) are vertically opposite.",
              "work": "\\angle BOC = \\angle FOE = 75^\\circ"
            }
          ]
